1
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:08,260
(Aoba University of the Arts)

2
00:00:16,233 --> 00:00:17,233
Good morning!

3
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:18,467
Morning.

4
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,600
Ouch...

5
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,033
Give me a break...

6
00:00:25,133 --> 00:00:26,400
Are you okay?

7
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:27,033
Are you hurt?

8
00:00:27,133 --> 00:00:28,367
Yeah.

9
00:00:28,667 --> 00:00:31,167
Thanks, you're a lifesaver.

10
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:38,820
"Hinata / The Overly Gentle Sun."

11
00:00:40,067 --> 00:00:42,667
Oh, don't mention it. I
should be thanking you.

12
00:00:43,267 --> 00:00:46,933
I'm so glad I got to see you again today.

13
00:00:47,033 --> 00:00:48,167
Really?

14
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:49,933
That's great.

15
00:00:50,433 --> 00:00:51,300
Are you okay?

16
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,733
Thanks.

17
00:00:52,933 --> 00:00:54,133
So... are you okay?

18
00:00:54,233 --> 00:00:55,567
I'm fine, I'm fine.

19
00:00:55,867 --> 00:00:59,100
Thank you, thank you.

20
00:01:00,567 --> 00:01:03,900
You're as sweet as ever, Hinata.

21
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,600
Oji Senpai.

22
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:13,400
"Oji / The President's Son."

23
00:01:14,467 --> 00:01:15,500
Hinata.

24
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:18,433
Here... please take this.

25
00:01:19,067 --> 00:01:20,300
Huh?

26
00:01:26,067 --> 00:01:27,333
Oh... I couldn't possibly.

27
00:01:27,433 --> 00:01:28,600
I can't accept this.

28
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:30,133
Just take it.

29
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,080
It's just a little something from me.

30
00:01:33,067 --> 00:01:34,300
What should I do?

31
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:35,867
Thank you.

32
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:40,167
Oh, by the way, tomorrow...

33
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:43,500
I'm sorry, my first
class is about to start.

34
00:01:44,367 --> 00:01:46,967
Thank you for this!

35
00:01:48,667 --> 00:01:49,867
Ah...

36
00:02:12,367 --> 00:02:14,600
Whoa! I'm so sorry...

37
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:24,433
That guy is Sora Senpai.

38
00:02:24,533 --> 00:02:27,067
His nickname is the "Tyrant Prince."

39
00:02:35,767 --> 00:02:36,833
(Sora / The Tyrant Prince)

40
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:40,133
There are a lot of rumors about him.

41
00:02:40,233 --> 00:02:43,267
Please go out with me!

42
00:02:45,867 --> 00:02:49,200
Even though he hates it
when people confess to him.

43
00:02:54,167 --> 00:02:56,500
He's still a student,
but he owns a nightclub.

44
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:59,500
I heard a lot of female
customers go there just for him.

45
00:03:02,767 --> 00:03:06,600
But he's got a short
temper and loves to fight.

46
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:08,267
No one dares to cross him.

47
00:03:09,933 --> 00:03:12,033
Everyone says he's terrifying.

48
00:03:14,667 --> 00:03:16,367
I'm dead.

49
00:03:26,333 --> 00:03:27,733
I'm sorry.

50
00:03:30,367 --> 00:03:31,733
Hey.

51
00:03:48,067 --> 00:03:49,333
That's enough.

52
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:51,733
I'm sorry.

53
00:03:51,833 --> 00:03:53,133
Watch where you're going.

54
00:03:56,733 --> 00:03:58,600
Oh, your shirt...

55
00:04:08,067 --> 00:04:12,300
♪ My mood goes up and down every day ♪

56
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:15,967
♪ Only time keeps slipping away ♪

57
00:04:16,067 --> 00:04:19,800
♪ This love has long surpassed friendship ♪

58
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:22,967
♪ This must be love ♪

59
00:04:23,067 --> 00:04:26,200
♪ This is my love ♪

60
00:04:26,467 --> 00:04:28,533
♪ On the campus slope ♪

61
00:04:28,633 --> 00:04:33,767
♪ We used to be nameless strangers ♪

62
00:04:33,867 --> 00:04:35,900
♪ The people passing by ♪

63
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:41,033
♪ Are all running
toward different futures ♪

64
00:04:41,133 --> 00:04:44,867
♪ After meeting you that summer ♪

65
00:04:44,967 --> 00:04:48,067
♪ Destiny began to turn ♪

66
00:04:48,167 --> 00:04:53,800
♪ Just go for it, yet I'm
still questioning myself ♪

67
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:54,467
♪ I can't say it out loud ♪

68
00:04:54,567 --> 00:04:58,733
♪ If this is love, it's hard to say ♪

69
00:04:58,833 --> 00:05:02,433
♪ What kind of expression
will you show tomorrow? ♪

70
00:05:02,533 --> 00:05:07,633
♪ This love is more than just friends ♪

71
00:05:07,733 --> 00:05:09,700
♪ This is love ♪

72
00:05:11,133 --> 00:05:12,567
"Your Sky Hare nochi Koi"

73
00:05:18,433 --> 00:05:20,100
(Episode 1: The Dangerous Senpai)

74
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:21,933
Didn't that scary senpai score big time?

75
00:05:22,033 --> 00:05:22,733
Here, for you.

76
00:05:22,833 --> 00:05:23,467
A rose.

77
00:05:23,567 --> 00:05:24,800
That's hilarious.

78
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:26,433
Really?

79
00:05:26,533 --> 00:05:27,833
Yeah.

80
00:05:27,933 --> 00:05:28,967
That being said.

81
00:05:29,067 --> 00:05:30,609
Didn't he tell you to
watch where you're going?

82
00:05:30,633 --> 00:05:32,233
Everyone says he's terrifying.

83
00:05:32,333 --> 00:05:33,767
But he's actually a nice guy.

84
00:05:33,867 --> 00:05:35,033
Nothing happened at all?

85
00:05:35,133 --> 00:05:37,800
I just told him to be careful.

86
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:39,167
Huh?

87
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:41,900
So your brother has a soft side after all.

88
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,033
My brother just looks intimidating.

89
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:52,400
"Riku / Sora's Younger Brother
A bit of a bad boy, but fiercely loyal."

90
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:00,900
"Ruito / Hinata's Best Friend
Always smiling."

91
00:06:01,433 --> 00:06:02,500
But still...

92
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:04,900
What if he comes after
you for revenge later?

93
00:06:07,133 --> 00:06:09,233
You'd better watch your
back on the way home.

94
00:06:09,333 --> 00:06:11,200
Stop it! That's not funny at all.

95
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:13,900
But... he was really scary
back there, wasn't he?

96
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:20,733
Excuse me.

97
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,100
Coming!

98
00:06:45,633 --> 00:06:46,900
I'm so sorry!

99
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,433
I really didn't mean to...

100
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:54,667
Even though he was
really scary at the time...

101
00:06:54,767 --> 00:06:56,533
But today was completely different.

102
00:06:56,633 --> 00:06:57,733
How so?

103
00:06:58,733 --> 00:07:02,267
Not a single drop of coffee got on me.

104
00:07:02,367 --> 00:07:05,433
It was almost like Senpai protected me.

105
00:07:05,533 --> 00:07:07,000
That wasn't a coincidence.

106
00:07:12,933 --> 00:07:14,433
It was probably just a fluke, right?

107
00:07:14,867 --> 00:07:17,333
His shirt... shouldn't I buy him a new one?

108
00:07:17,433 --> 00:07:19,333
Uh... my brother probably doesn't care.

109
00:07:19,433 --> 00:07:20,533
No...

110
00:07:20,633 --> 00:07:23,833
You definitely have to replace it!

111
00:07:23,933 --> 00:07:26,433
Wait, which one is it?

112
00:07:30,533 --> 00:07:31,867
Ah!

113
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:36,533
How about I just sneak a new one to him?

114
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:45,167
Oh crap, oh crap.

115
00:07:45,633 --> 00:07:46,800
(Hanamura)

116
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:48,367
Ah, this is it!

117
00:07:49,867 --> 00:07:51,167
Huh?

118
00:07:51,633 --> 00:07:53,033
Hinata?

119
00:08:01,133 --> 00:08:04,200
What's up? Don't tell me...

120
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:06,400
You came looking for me?

121
00:08:06,767 --> 00:08:08,933
Uh...

122
00:08:09,667 --> 00:08:11,433
Ah! I think I'm in the wrong place.

123
00:08:14,033 --> 00:08:17,467
Earlier... I forgot to tell you something.

124
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:19,933
What is it?

125
00:08:20,033 --> 00:08:23,367
You see, tomorrow is my birthday.

126
00:08:24,333 --> 00:08:26,933
So I'm hoping you can
make it again this year, Hinata.

127
00:08:27,033 --> 00:08:29,400
But... I...

128
00:08:31,367 --> 00:08:33,267
It's going to be a blast.

129
00:08:33,367 --> 00:08:34,367
I promise.

130
00:08:36,667 --> 00:08:38,233
Um...

131
00:08:39,300 --> 00:08:40,800
What do you say?

132
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:42,133
Will you come?

133
00:08:47,433 --> 00:08:49,433
What's... this?

134
00:08:49,533 --> 00:08:51,567
Nothing... this is...

135
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:53,133
What?

136
00:08:53,233 --> 00:08:54,433
A shirt?

137
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:55,733
That's so tacky.

138
00:08:55,833 --> 00:08:57,133
You really are...

139
00:08:58,200 --> 00:09:00,800
Ah... um... I'll be there.

140
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:02,033
Really?

141
00:09:02,133 --> 00:09:03,567
Awesome!

142
00:09:08,167 --> 00:09:09,600
Thanks.

143
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:11,833
Okay.

144
00:09:24,467 --> 00:09:26,000
Good work, everyone.

145
00:09:29,833 --> 00:09:32,133
It's rare to see Sora get his shirt dirty.

146
00:09:32,233 --> 00:09:33,867
And it's completely ruined.

147
00:09:40,467 --> 00:09:41,947
"Makoto / Sora's Partner / Reliable."

148
00:09:48,633 --> 00:09:50,753
"Tasuku / Sora's Best Friend
/ Innocent and carefree."

149
00:09:53,133 --> 00:09:55,000
You're as clumsy as ever.

150
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:56,933
Am not. I'm nothing like you.

151
00:09:57,033 --> 00:09:58,333
Huh? That's so mean.

152
00:09:59,667 --> 00:10:01,033
Are you a kid?

153
00:10:12,433 --> 00:10:13,433
What's wrong?

154
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:38,967
Um...

155
00:10:50,833 --> 00:10:52,033
Your shoelace.

156
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:54,667
Honestly.

157
00:10:54,767 --> 00:10:57,167
You really are as clumsy as ever.

158
00:10:57,267 --> 00:10:58,900
Hurry up and organize your locker.

159
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,500
I am organizing it!

160
00:11:04,767 --> 00:11:05,967
Oops.

161
00:11:06,067 --> 00:11:07,200
Let's go.

162
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,967
That was close...

163
00:11:26,767 --> 00:11:29,600
Wait, you're going to Oji's birthday party?

164
00:11:29,700 --> 00:11:32,267
Well, given the situation earlier...

165
00:11:33,167 --> 00:11:34,927
You really don't know
how to say no, do you?

166
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,833
I've never seen you turn
anyone down, Hinata.

167
00:11:37,933 --> 00:11:39,733
You always give people false hope.

168
00:11:39,833 --> 00:11:41,867
That's why Oji
keeps pushing his luck.

169
00:11:41,967 --> 00:11:43,767
I just don't know how to say no...

170
00:11:43,867 --> 00:11:44,700
Huh?

171
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:46,776
If you don't want to go,
just say "I don't want to."

172
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:48,833
But that might hurt his feelings...

173
00:11:48,933 --> 00:11:50,500
Ugh, seriously.

174
00:11:51,233 --> 00:11:54,033
You're way too nice for your own good.

175
00:11:56,867 --> 00:11:58,333
You're helpless.

176
00:11:58,433 --> 00:11:59,300
Huh?

177
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:00,433
I'll go with you!

178
00:12:00,533 --> 00:12:01,433
You'll come with me?

179
00:12:01,533 --> 00:12:02,700
Yeah.

180
00:12:03,033 --> 00:12:06,900
I... have somewhere to be, so I'll pass.

181
00:12:11,533 --> 00:12:12,533
Where are you going?

182
00:12:12,633 --> 00:12:13,833
I don't know.

183
00:13:06,533 --> 00:13:08,700
Dad, congratulations on your promotion!

184
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:14,667
Thank you! I'm so happy.

185
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:17,733
Come on, stop it.

186
00:13:17,833 --> 00:13:19,233
I'm not a kid anymore.

187
00:13:19,333 --> 00:13:22,300
In a parent's eyes, their
child is always a child.

188
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:24,600
How old do you think I am!

189
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:27,700
Hinano helped me pick that out too, right?

190
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:28,633
Yeah.

191
00:13:28,733 --> 00:13:30,700
What about me?

192
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:33,300
How old do you think you are?

193
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:37,600
Huh? Didn't you just say
a child is always a child?

194
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:38,900
Yeah, exactly.

195
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,867
That's right! Alright,
let's have a sumo match.

196
00:13:41,967 --> 00:13:44,067
- Alright!
- Bring it on!

197
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:46,333
Whoa!

198
00:13:46,967 --> 00:13:48,433
Go, go!

199
00:13:48,533 --> 00:13:50,300
Awesome!

200
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:11,133
Happy birthday!

201
00:14:11,233 --> 00:14:12,433
Cheers!

202
00:14:13,267 --> 00:14:14,400
How old are you now?

203
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:15,867
Twenty-two.

204
00:14:21,733 --> 00:14:23,467
Wow!

205
00:14:23,567 --> 00:14:24,833
Whoa!

206
00:14:27,167 --> 00:14:28,667
Oh! Hinata!

207
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:31,733
Senpai.

208
00:14:31,833 --> 00:14:33,700
Here's a gift from us.

209
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:35,833
Thank you.

210
00:14:35,933 --> 00:14:37,100
But...

211
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:41,400
I'm just happy you came, Hinata.

212
00:14:47,067 --> 00:14:48,200
Cheers!

213
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:48,833
Cheers!

214
00:14:48,906 --> 00:14:51,240
Let's all raise a glass!

215
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:56,033
Awesome.

216
00:15:01,867 --> 00:15:04,533
Let's all toast!

217
00:15:04,633 --> 00:15:06,667
Cheers...

218
00:15:07,267 --> 00:15:09,233
- Congratulations!
- Thanks.

219
00:15:09,333 --> 00:15:12,133
Ah... Hinata can't drink.

220
00:15:12,233 --> 00:15:13,467
I know.

221
00:15:13,567 --> 00:15:15,100
So I got him a non-alcoholic one.

222
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:16,367
But...

223
00:15:16,867 --> 00:15:18,867
If you're worried, why
don't you try it first?

224
00:15:19,967 --> 00:15:21,100
Okay.

225
00:15:25,767 --> 00:15:27,033
How is it?

226
00:15:27,333 --> 00:15:29,133
It's non-alcoholic.

227
00:15:29,233 --> 00:15:30,567
See?

228
00:15:30,667 --> 00:15:33,333
Here, Hinata, you drink too.

229
00:15:41,733 --> 00:15:42,733
It's so good.

230
00:15:42,833 --> 00:15:44,067
We have plenty more today.

231
00:15:44,167 --> 00:15:45,033
Drink up.

232
00:15:45,133 --> 00:15:46,267
Down the hatch.

233
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,233
Cheers!

234
00:16:04,333 --> 00:16:06,000
Cheers...

235
00:16:09,167 --> 00:16:10,633
So good!

236
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:28,100
Is it good?

237
00:16:28,733 --> 00:16:30,100
That's great.

238
00:16:34,467 --> 00:16:36,000
Hey, are you okay?

239
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:37,433
Are you alright?

240
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:46,733
Are you okay?

241
00:16:51,967 --> 00:16:55,100
What's wrong? Your face is so red.

242
00:16:56,133 --> 00:16:57,567
Yeah...

243
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:14,333
Sora.

244
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:15,633
Call him Boss.

245
00:17:15,733 --> 00:17:17,533
Alright, alright, Boss.

246
00:17:17,633 --> 00:17:19,333
Business is booming today too.

247
00:17:22,767 --> 00:17:24,533
Are they here again?

248
00:17:24,633 --> 00:17:25,333
Drink up!

249
00:17:25,433 --> 00:17:27,500
One glass isn't enough!

250
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:28,133
Chug, chug, chug!

251
00:17:28,233 --> 00:17:30,267
Bring it over already.

252
00:17:30,367 --> 00:17:32,400
I heard it's Oji's birthday party today.

253
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:34,652
Just because he's the principal's son...
he thinks he can do whatever he wants.

254
00:17:34,676 --> 00:17:35,263
Hey.

255
00:17:35,967 --> 00:17:37,633
What? I'm not wrong.

256
00:17:38,533 --> 00:17:42,567
Yeah... they are being a bit too loud.

257
00:17:42,590 --> 00:17:44,123
See?

258
00:17:44,300 --> 00:17:46,000
What should we do, Boss?

259
00:17:47,933 --> 00:17:53,767
Happy birthday to you.

260
00:17:53,867 --> 00:17:57,233
Happy birthday, dear Oji.

261
00:17:57,333 --> 00:18:01,633
Happy birthday to you.

262
00:18:01,733 --> 00:18:04,667
Happy birthday, Oji!

263
00:18:12,833 --> 00:18:16,233
Why don't you make a wish
in front of everyone?

264
00:18:19,033 --> 00:18:20,133
Make a wish!

265
00:18:21,467 --> 00:18:22,667
Go out with me.

266
00:18:23,333 --> 00:18:24,200
Huh?

267
00:18:24,300 --> 00:18:26,267
Wait, seriously?

268
00:18:27,467 --> 00:18:32,267
I... put a lot of effort
into today for you, Hinata.

269
00:18:32,367 --> 00:18:36,000
You're not going to... reject me, are you?

270
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:39,533
Um...

271
00:18:39,633 --> 00:18:42,467
You accepted my gift, right?

272
00:18:42,567 --> 00:18:46,033
And today too...

273
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:49,200
No... that's...

274
00:18:51,133 --> 00:18:53,667
Don't embarrass me in front of everyone.

275
00:18:57,667 --> 00:18:59,300
No, stop it!

276
00:19:01,733 --> 00:19:03,304
This is scary...

277
00:19:03,994 --> 00:19:05,119
Someone stop him!

278
00:19:07,467 --> 00:19:08,933
I can't move.

279
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,867
No, help!

280
00:19:20,167 --> 00:19:21,533
What are you doing?!

281
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:26,767
You wanna stick your nose in this?

282
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:29,600
That's right.

283
00:19:29,667 --> 00:19:30,767
Huh?

284
00:19:33,567 --> 00:19:36,700
This guy is... dating me.

285
00:19:46,267 --> 00:19:47,267
Huh?

286
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,600
What?

287
00:19:50,867 --> 00:19:52,167
What are you talking about?

288
00:20:01,567 --> 00:20:02,967
Let's go.

289
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:05,667
Hold on! Hey!

290
00:20:06,833 --> 00:20:08,667
Excuse me, did something happen?

291
00:20:11,100 --> 00:20:12,567
That jerk...

292
00:20:16,667 --> 00:20:17,800
Ugh...

293
00:20:18,367 --> 00:20:20,100
My head hurts...

294
00:20:20,567 --> 00:20:22,767
Senpai, let me go!

295
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:24,700
Hey...

296
00:20:25,833 --> 00:20:27,533
Are you okay?

297
00:20:33,667 --> 00:20:35,300
What's wrong?

298
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:37,767
Hop on.

299
00:20:38,833 --> 00:20:40,467
I don't want to.

300
00:20:41,167 --> 00:20:42,800
Why...

301
00:20:43,233 --> 00:20:44,367
Hurry up.

302
00:20:44,467 --> 00:20:46,567
I'm heavy.

303
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:51,000
It's dangerous.

304
00:20:51,367 --> 00:20:52,633
Just get on.

305
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,300
You're so annoying.

306
00:21:05,233 --> 00:21:07,133
I'm taking you home today.

307
00:21:11,033 --> 00:21:12,267
Dad...

308
00:21:13,733 --> 00:21:15,133
Huh?

309
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:20,833
Huh... did you change your fabric softener?

310
00:21:32,067 --> 00:21:35,067
You came to pick me up, Dad...

311
00:21:35,767 --> 00:21:37,400
I told you, I'm not your dad.

312
00:21:38,933 --> 00:21:42,967
You used to carry me on
your back a lot when I was little.

313
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:46,700
But things are different now.

314
00:21:49,833 --> 00:21:52,767
I'm not a kid anymore.

315
00:21:55,600 --> 00:21:58,067
Stop treating me like a kid!

316
00:22:00,400 --> 00:22:01,400
Put me down!

317
00:22:01,467 --> 00:22:02,567
Stop squirming.

318
00:22:02,667 --> 00:22:03,833
It's dangerous...

319
00:22:03,933 --> 00:22:05,700
- I said it's dangerous!
- Hurry up!

320
00:22:07,067 --> 00:22:09,200
I knew it was dangerous.

321
00:22:11,767 --> 00:22:13,100
Watch out!

322
00:22:17,867 --> 00:22:19,733
Hey! Are you okay?

323
00:22:19,833 --> 00:22:21,600
I'm not a kid.

324
00:22:28,033 --> 00:22:31,500
But... I want to too.

325
00:22:34,233 --> 00:22:38,833
You could at least kiss my forehead.

326
00:22:42,567 --> 00:22:43,733
Hmph!

327
00:22:43,833 --> 00:22:46,267
You kiss my sister.

328
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:50,233
What are you talking about?

329
00:22:52,567 --> 00:22:57,633
Sigh... you'd never do that to me anyway.

330
00:23:00,433 --> 00:23:01,700
Ah.

331
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:04,067
The stars are so beautiful.

332
00:23:09,467 --> 00:23:10,767
I...

333
00:23:10,867 --> 00:23:12,833
I love the sky the most.

334
00:24:44,633 --> 00:24:47,076
(Next Episode Preview) What did
you mean by what you did yesterday?

335
00:24:47,100 --> 00:24:48,233
Wait.

336
00:24:48,333 --> 00:24:49,667
You're dating this guy?

337
00:24:49,767 --> 00:24:51,767
That's right, we're dating.

338
00:24:51,867 --> 00:24:53,827
(A Fake Couple is Born)
This is our little secret.

339
00:24:53,867 --> 00:24:54,600
Looking forward to this, Hinata.

340
00:24:54,700 --> 00:24:56,900
Isn't the distance between
you two a bit weird?

341
00:25:05,567 --> 00:25:06,933
Likewise.

342
00:25:08,233 --> 00:25:12,633
I've... always been one
with nature like this.

343
00:25:14,067 --> 00:25:16,600
How's that? Pretty cool, right?

344
00:25:17,700 --> 00:25:18,700
Is it me?

345
00:25:18,767 --> 00:25:19,633
Me?

346
00:25:19,733 --> 00:25:21,533
How is it?

347
00:25:30,533 --> 00:25:31,733
It's actually pretty good.

348
00:25:31,833 --> 00:25:33,100
Great.

349
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:34,100
And the weather is perfect too.

350
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:36,200
It'll definitely go
viral once it's released.

351
00:25:36,967 --> 00:25:39,733
You're related to a superstar, after all.

352
00:25:42,767 --> 00:25:44,433
You two are super cute.

353
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:51,133
Make sure to watch episode two!

354
00:25:53,900 --> 00:25:54,900
Okay!
